{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition","id":1198700,"title":"Belial's Brood in 2nd Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-23T09:16:05-07:00","id":1198700,"title":"Belial's Brood in 2nd Edition","content":"I'm currently running my first ever Vampire; The Requiem 2e campaign. I'm new to 2e but I have plenty of 1e experience as a player. I currently only own the Chronicles of Darkness core book, the Vampire; The Requiem 2e core book and the Half-Damned book. So far it seems they got completely rid of Belial's Brood. At least I can't find anything about them.<br /> <br /> Does Belial's Brood still exist in VTR 2e and if yes, where can I find more information on what they're like in 2e?<br /> <br /> <br /> Second and most important question:<br /> <br /> I had a crazy idea. I wanted to introduce Belial's Brood to my VTR 2e campaign, but not as Satanists, but a Strix worshippers. Would that work and does that make sense? How would I go about introducing a Strix-worshipping Belial's Brood in my campaign, an already ongoing campaign?<br /> <br /> To clarify: The campaign starts in 1888 London in which I used Jack the Ripper as the hook for the campaign (the Ripper in our campaign turned out to be the Strix named Anna Red). The players started as mortal humans investigating the Ripper case. They got in contact with the Kindred as well as the Malleus Maleficarum. The party of humans (some of them ghouls) proved themselves useful to the Kindred so the Kindred embraced them. That's where we currently are in the campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":".  Added a bit of extra info. 03-23-2018, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:04:46-07:00","id":1198727,"title":"","content":"While they were not mentioned yet in 2e, it was confirmed by the previous developer that they are still around (even though that with the change of developers, nothing is certain). It doesn't yet change the fact that, as I said at the beginning, there is no official information about the Brood, so you could play them in any way you want (infernalists, strix worshipers, VII or whatever else you have in mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T10:30:24-07:00","id":1198739,"title":"","content":"I've been reading through the 1e brood book with the intent of making them as a mystery cult (or six) and being Strix worshipers makes a lot of sense given how many Strix want similar things from kindred as the brood do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:01:11-07:00","id":1198757,"title":"","content":"I think this makes perfect sense. As far as I understand their incomprehensible motivations, the Strux are generally pissed off with kindred for failing to appreciate the gifts of the Beast. They cling to their Humanity. Pathetic. And, in essence, that\u2019s the same basic fault the 1e Brood found in the All Night Society.<br /> <br /> I will steal your idea for future reference, good sir. Cheers.<br /> <br /> Edit: might as well start spit balling<br /> <br /> Cult initiation - the Brood<br /> 1 gain the Occult (Stryx) specialty<br /> 2 gain Atrocious 1 merit<br /> 3 gain Indomitable 2 merit<br /> 4 gain Riding the Wave 3<br /> 5 by spendimg 3 vitae you may regain 1 willpower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 03-23-2018, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:31:53-07:00","id":1198775,"title":"","content":"So far all we got was the Pledge to the Worthless One in Secrets of the Covenants. It was publicly made available <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZXnaJDf-gERGZe97JoIqj2bffJyrjal8Ch4xWD4L9lg/edit#heading=h.kkeeygpnslef\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> during the open development sequence. We've been told they still exist, and it stands to reason (it looks like there's a lot more covenants than in 1e, or even than the 2e books make out), we just haven't seen them.<br /> <br /> Pledge to the Worthless One (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Target number of successes: 8<br /> Sacrament: A person content with his life<br /> This ritual is considered heretical to all mainstream Lancea et Sanctum creeds. It calls on the force of the devil Belial \u2013 the Worthless one \u2013 to gift upon a vampire his dark blessings. The subject of this ritual swears herself to Belial, and slays the sacramental mortal. She must consent to its effects for the ritual to take effect, but once it\u2019s taken effect, it cannot be ended by any known practice. Part of the oath requires the vampire pledge her immortal soul after her Final Death. This is largely academic, as no vampire knows what happens to a vampire after the Requiem\u2019s end. The pledge affords a number of effects:<br /> \u2022 The subject chooses one of the seven deadly sins with which to ally; greed, pride, wrath, sloth, gluttony, envy, or lust. From that point forward, every Vitae she draws from a mortal in the throes of that sin is doubled. Characters not exhibiting those sins provide her half the nourishment; she takes only one from each two Vitae drawn.<br /> \u2022 She gains the advantages of frenzy at all times, even while completely lucid.<br /> \u2022 She cannot maintain a Touchstone.<br /> \u2022 She exhibits one physical sign of damnation. This may manifest as cloven hooves, a third nipple, or any other classic sign of diabolism.<br /> \u2022 She gains a familiar. This is a demon in an animal\u2019s flesh. It counts as a five dot Retainer, with three dots of Disciplines. She can see through its eyes, and speak through its mouth.<br /> \u2022 Any member of the Lancea et Sanctum is honor-bound to destroy her if her pledge is uncovered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-24T16:12:35-07:00","id":1199242,"title":"","content":"I think Rose Bailey confirmed that the Brood still exist in Vampire The Requiem (along with everything in 1e that didn't get officially converted) though I understand why they shied away from introducing them in 2e, they were basically a method of including Sabbat-esque antagonists to VTR to be familiar with players coming from VTM, and since 2e tried to distance itself from VTM as much as possible the change is not surprising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T14:52:17-07:00","id":1199488,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies everyone.<br /> <br /> I'm convinced now. I'm going to use Belial's Brood as a covenant of Strix worshippers. They are going to be the new kids on the block in my campaign. I even wrote a little splat text for them:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Most Kindred don't pay attention to the bottom of the barrel, those who are unaligned in the All Night Society. Most ancilla think they are little more than a nuisance, rebel scum unable or unwilling to join a covenant, weak, pathetic. Most elders forgot they even exist. But many neonates who don't have the luxury of a well-kept herd or a fertile feeding ground will often come in contact with the unaligned during their hunt for blood. These Neonates know that something sinister is brewing among the unaligned.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;What is humanity? Most sires will tell their childer that humanity is all that stands between their sanity and the Beast. It is the one thing that keeps the beast at bay. But why would you want to keep the beast at bay? After all, your beast has so much more to offer than your humanity. By clinging to your humanity and denying your beast, you are denying your true potential, and for what? So you can keep your human morals? Your human emotions? Your human soul? Why would you want to do that? Do these traits make you a better hunter? Get it through your thick skull neonate, you aren't human anymore. You are a predator now, and predators shouldn't act like their prey.&quot; </b><br /> <br /> This is what the Birds of Dis tried to teach the Kindred. Most Kindred didn't listen, they instead try to live among their prey by pretending to be like them, much to the disgust of the Strix. Most Striges have given up on the Kindred and regard them as little more than prey. But one Strix decided to give the Kindred another chance. He decided to reach out to the Kindred, but he only made his presence known to those who felt alienated by the All Night Society. He approached the weak and beaten down, he approached the isolated Kindred hungering for power and revenge. He approached the Kindred who felt alienated by their human cousins. He approached the outcasts, the filth, the undesirables, the freaks, the forgotten. These Kindred formed the heart and core of a new covenant, a covenant under the leadership of the Strix. They called themselves Belial's Brood, the Worthless Ones. It was a fitting name. It pleased the Strix.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T00:06:14-07:00","id":1199612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1198775#post1198775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 She cannot maintain a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, can't believe I didn't notice this before -- wouldn't they just all fall asleep in a few weeks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T04:01:05-07:00","id":1199649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1199612#post1199612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, can't believe I didn't notice this before -- wouldn't they just all fall asleep in a few weeks?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recently learned there\u2019s a difference between a lost/dead Touchstone and a detached one. Presumably this bit refers to a vampire not being able to keep an attachment to their Touchstones, which still is different from losing them. S/he has them, the merit, but simply doesn\u2019t or is unable to interact with them in a meaningful way, i.e. Languid need not apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:20:16-07:00","id":1199690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1199612#post1199612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, can't believe I didn't notice this before -- wouldn't they just all fall asleep in a few weeks?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first time, sure. After that, the consequences of making every detachment roll with a -2 penalty, being short one possible Anchor, and not having a way to clear the Tainted Condition or get talked down from frenzy serve as fairly ample consequences for walking around without a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T06:25:17-07:00","id":1199693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1199690#post1199690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first time, sure. After that, the consequences of making every detachment roll with a -2 penalty, being short one possible Anchor, and not having a way to clear the Tainted Condition or get talked down from frenzy serve as fairly ample consequences for walking around without a Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tainted Condition has nothing to do with Touchstones. It fades through time and/or taking aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T10:58:04-07:00","id":1199764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1199693#post1199693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tainted Condition has nothing to do with Touchstones. It fades through time and/or taking aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026I meant the <i>Tempted</i> Condition, which is two items down from Tainted in the Condition listing, shares four of seven letters with its name, and has three Resolution criteria, of which &quot;Have a meaningful connection with a Touchstone&quot; is the only one that does not have potentially or not-even-potentially murderous implications. Typos happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:03:40-07:00","id":1199765,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry if I came off condescending. I just tried to correct a mistake I saw to save people some confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T00:31:46-07:00","id":1202476,"title":"","content":"I remember someone back in the day running the Brood as the demon Belial's pet project on earth. That's an angle I kind of liked and would probably try to run with if I would run Requiem in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:36:02-07:00","id":1202799,"title":"","content":"I don't think i'm doing Belial's Brood very differently from the books or most people, but i have the Brood be functionnaly 2 groups.<br /> The first is what i call the teenagers (no relation to the actual age of the vampire). They are what most people picture. Basically evil for evil sakes (or rather monstrous for the sake of being a monster). They dont last long (typically).<br /> There is another group tho. They are subtly embedded within all of the covenants. They take many forms, but they all have the same end goal. They want to remove humanity as a consideration but without becoming mindless. Essentially they want to be at humanity 0 but not become a draugr of have any of the other problems associated with a low humanity.<br /> <br /> Striges (is that the plural?) love either group depending on the individual and they often form types of partnerships.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:03:57-07:00","id":1204002,"title":"","content":"I thought Belial's Brood was an excellent product - but yes they may have been a Sabbat-like holdover from Masquerade which they want to put distance between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T07:39:08-07:00","id":1204542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1202799#post1202799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think i'm doing Belial's Brood very differently from the books or most people, but i have the Brood be functionnaly 2 groups.<br /> The first is what i call the teenagers (no relation to the actual age of the vampire). They are what most people picture. Basically evil for evil sakes (or rather monstrous for the sake of being a monster). They dont last long (typically).<br /> There is another group tho. They are subtly embedded within all of the covenants. They take many forms, but they all have the same end goal. They want to remove humanity as a consideration but without becoming mindless. Essentially they want to be at humanity 0 but not become a draugr of have any of the other problems associated with a low humanity.<br /> <br /> Striges (is that the plural?) love either group depending on the individual and they often form types of partnerships.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is quite similar, although rather than teenagers being a group within the covenant, they\u2019re basically Sabat Shovelheads. And the proper Brood are very much like vampire eqivalent of Bale Hounds. A secret 6th Covenant of Infernalists that infiltrates the others to corrupt who they can and cause discord among those they can\u2019t. They don\u2019t directly worship the Stirges, but many find their embrace the monster philosophy speaks to them, and Stirges generally find the Brood very entertaining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T21:17:04-07:00","id":1205458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1204542#post1204542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My take is quite similar, although rather than teenagers being a group within the covenant, they\u2019re basically Sabat Shovelheads. And the proper Brood are very much like vampire eqivalent of Bale Hounds. A secret 6th Covenant of Infernalists that infiltrates the others to corrupt who they can and cause discord among those they can\u2019t. They don\u2019t directly worship the Stirges, but many find their embrace the monster philosophy speaks to them, and Stirges generally find the Brood very entertaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that Theban Ritual related to Belial, the Brood as infiltrators make even more sense. The Sanctified who revels in their damnation. The Acolyte who indulge themselves with blood sacrifice. The Dragon whose experiments debase instead of exalt. The Firebrand who turns to violence over governance. The Invictus who turns the system of society into an engine of oppression. Philosophies of each Covenant, taken into an extreme and no longer merely inhuman but atrocious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T21:41:26-07:00","id":1205460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205458#post1205458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With that Theban Ritual related to Belial, the Brood as infiltrators make even more sense. The Sanctified who revels in their damnation. The Acolyte who indulge themselves with blood sacrifice. The Dragon whose experiments debase instead of exalt. The Firebrand who turns to violence over governance. The Invictus who turns the system of society into an engine of oppression. Philosophies of each Covenant, taken into an extreme and no longer merely inhuman but atrocious.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was exactly what inspired my take on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T23:21:49-07:00","id":1205476,"title":"","content":"I should note that the whole Covenant situation in my Chronicles is a little different than the default assumptions, with a lot of inspiration from Danae Macabre\u2019s global versions of the Covenants as well as Masquerade\u2019s Sects. My setting has two to four factions roughly analogous to Masquerade\u2019s Sects, depending on how you count (the lines between them aren\u2019t as hard as they are in Masquerade):<br /> <br /> The New Camarilla (or \u201cNeo-Cam\u201d) is made up of the Invictus, who are a bit closer to the Danse Macabre\u2019s Prima Invicta, and the Lancea et Sanctum, with the optional sidebar from their Covenant book about the Cardinals as a global council in play. The Lancea et Sanctum interpret the Traditions and the Invictus enforce them. <br /> <br /> Ostensibly allied to the New Camarilla is the Ordo Dracul, who serve a similar role to the Tremere. They submit to Neo Cam law but serve their own interests and have their own internal power structures, and behind the scenes actually hold a lot of influence over Neo Cam politics - it\u2019s an open secret that a majority of the most powerful Invictus also hold partial status in the Ordo Dracul, though the conflict of interest is not often publicly questioned for fear of retribution.<br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement combines aspects of Masquerade\u2019s Anarch Movement and Danse Macabre\u2019s Commonwealth. A movement of New Camarilla sepratists seeking to establish an alternative form of kindred government. On uneasy but not outright hostile terms with the New Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone is a bit like a softened take on the Sabat, being a \u201cSect\u201d that rejects the New Camarilla\u2019s Traditions in favor of \u201cdo what thou wilt.\u201d Often allied with the Carthian Movement in their opposition to the New Camarilla, but ultimately rejecting their experimental forms of government as well.<br /> <br /> Belial\u2019s Brood takes over the harder side of the Sabat and sprinkles in a dash of Baali infernalism, and infiltrates all of the other Covenants. Within Neo-Cam Domains, they generally take the form of a cult within the Lancea et Sanctum, which is where the Pledge to the Worthless One Ritual comes from. Within the Ordo Dracul, they\u2019ve created a secret sub-order which is pretty much the Devil\u2019s Eye from Danse Macabre. In Carthian Domains, they manipulate the experiments to their own ends, or else stir up discontent to sabatoge experiments (I\u2019ll admit, I feel like this part needs further development). And within the Circle of the Crone they take advantage of the lack of Traditions and go full Sabat.<br /> <br /> VII\u2019s identity I\u2019m undecided on. I like the Akhud a lot and they definitely exist in my setting, but I\u2019m not 100% sold on them being VII. Maybe I\u2019ll look into Masquerade\u2019s Black Hand for inspiration. Or play with the Strix Chronicle\u2019s suggestion that they are somehow connected with the Stirges, with attacks always occurring within 72 hours of a confirmed Strix sighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-11-2018, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:25:25-07:00","id":1205545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205460#post1205460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was exactly what inspired my take on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205476#post1205476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VII\u2019s identity I\u2019m undecided on. I like the Akhud a lot and they definitely exist in my setting, but I\u2019m not 100% sold on them being VII. Maybe I\u2019ll look into Masquerade\u2019s Black Hand for inspiration. Or play with the Strix Chronicle\u2019s suggestion that they are somehow connected with the Stirges, with attacks always occurring within 72 hours of a confirmed Strix sighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had an idea i'm playing with. It hasnt come up in my chronicle so i can still change it.<br /> I am rather fond of parallels and opposites. So if i have a Belials Brood that stands hidden within the covenants with the goal of getting rid safely of humanity, i want a group with a somewhat opposite agenda. My idea is that, equally hidden within the covenants (at varying degree) there is a group who wants to become human again. Now i called them VII, but honestly thats because i'm not using VII and i couldnt find a suitable name. Also i liked the idea that the mysterious kills of VII were actually a form of mercy kill that a member can ask for if they feel that they are losing the fight against the beast.<br /> <br /> And to circle back more to the purpose of the thread. Belials Brood is fiercely opposed to this group (and vice versa).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 04-11-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T07:55:50-07:00","id":1205592,"title":"","content":"Similar question. Has any information on VII been brought around again in 2e? I don't think there has but I may have missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T08:53:23-07:00","id":1205614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205592#post1205592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar question. Has any information on VII been brought around again in 2e? I don't think there has but I may have missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a chapter dedicated to them in the core rule book of Vampire The Requiem. Look at pages 47 to 49. It isn't much, but it should be enough to give you inspiration on how to run VII in 2e.<br /> <br /> They're basically similar to their 1e counterpart, except they're related to the Strix now. How? That's up to you to decide. They could be Strix-possessed; or they could be the opposite: they could be vampires who hunt down other vampires who are Strix-possessed. Or perhaps they are the machinations of the God-Machine? These are all possibilities brought up in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T13:42:16-07:00","id":1205739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205592#post1205592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar question. Has any information on VII been brought around again in 2e? I don't think there has but I may have missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the Cerberus Pact from the elder's book was a potential VII candidate, and the book also updated the Akhud as a clan. Beyond that there is the small chapter dedicated to them in the core book, like Ventrue Life said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T13:48:44-07:00","id":1205740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205739#post1205739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe the Cerberus Pact from the elder's book was a potential VII candidate, and the book also updated the Akhud as a clan. Beyond that there is the small chapter dedicated to them in the core book, like Ventrue Life said.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I think the canonizing of the Akhud in 2e actually makes them a <i>less</i> likely candidate for VII. If they\u2019re a Clan that definitely existed and are known of by the other Clans, even if what is thought to be known about them is largely misinformation, it takes away a bit of the mystery surrounding VII if it\u2019s them.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why I\u2019m not sold on them as VII. They were my favorite version of VII, and I couldn\u2019t be happier that 2e made them canon. But it also makes me want VII to be something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:07:35-07:00","id":1205748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205740#post1205740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, I think the canonizing of the Akhud in 2e actually makes them a <i>less</i> likely candidate for VII. If they\u2019re a Clan that definitely existed and are known of by the other Clans, even if what is thought to be known about them is largely misinformation, it takes away a bit of the mystery surrounding VII if it\u2019s them.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why I\u2019m not sold on them as VII. They were my favorite version of VII, and I couldn\u2019t be happier that 2e made them canon. But it also makes me want VII to be something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see where you're coming from. I'm personally of the opinion that the VII covenant is less of a covenant and more of a memetic idea that the Kindred created. The idea of Kindred hunting other kindred isn't out of the question, and the reasons are innumerable. In my games, if VII crops up it is just a group of Kindred (or various other vampires) that took up the symbol of VII as a terror tactic, and to give themselves some unification; kindred like their history, and the idea of being a part of an ancient covenant of terrifying vampire killers would probably feed their ego. I also generally justify the VII symbol to have the same purpose of a stylized S; easy to mark down and isn't too much of a time waster.<br /> <br /> Of course, if people wanna run VII as some conspiracy their isn't a problem with that; the idea does hold merit. I just find the idea that VII as an idea is more scary because you can destroy an organization, but to destroy an idea among a group of immortals who love to gossip is significantly a harder challenge.<br /> <br /> I also like to use the memetic idea because in 2e Invictus Oaths and Carthian Laws are just essentially ideas being written down and spread about, but they still hold mystic power. It gives me plenty of plot ideas for what might happen to a local group of Kindred taking up the VII symbol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:29:43-07:00","id":1205754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205748#post1205748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I can see where you're coming from. I'm personally of the opinion that the VII covenant is less of a covenant and more of a memetic idea that the Kindred created. The idea of Kindred hunting other kindred isn't out of the question, and the reasons are innumerable. In my games, if VII crops up it is just a group of Kindred (or various other vampires) that took up the symbol of VII as a terror tactic, and to give themselves some unification; kindred like their history, and the idea of being a part of an ancient covenant of terrifying vampire killers would probably feed their ego. I also generally justify the VII symbol to have the same purpose of a stylized S; easy to mark down and isn't too much of a time waster.<br /> <br /> Of course, if people wanna run VII as some conspiracy their isn't a problem with that; the idea does hold merit. I just find the idea that VII as an idea is more scary because you can destroy an organization, but to destroy an idea among a group of immortals who love to gossip is significantly a harder challenge.<br /> <br /> I also like to use the memetic idea because in 2e Invictus Oaths and Carthian Laws are just essentially ideas being written down and spread about, but they still hold mystic power. It gives me plenty of plot ideas for what might happen to a local group of Kindred taking up the VII symbol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. I imagine that even in settings where VII is a proper covenant, they get a lot of copycats, to the point where <i>most</i> VII murders turn out to be false leads. I like the idea of a lot of vampires taking that to mean that there is no VII. Which, of course, the real VII uses to its advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:33:27-07:00","id":1205757,"title":"","content":"Personally, the Betrayed are my favorite version of VII, but actually in my head canon, VII is more of an umbrella term for a number of secretive organizations which hunt after vampires, each for its own reason. The eight main covenants are Cerberus Pact, the Betrayed, the Tenth Choir, the Iltani (which are a covenant in my setting), Legio Mortem, Weihan Cynn, Conspiracy of Seers (a modern incarnation of the Cult of Augurs) and the Blood of Ahran (there is a seperating between the Akhud and the covenant in my setting, so while many Akhud join the Blood, it is not the default). They are called &quot;the Seven and the One&quot;, and of course each of them claims to be the &quot;One&quot; and the rest as the &quot;Seven&quot;. Of course, most of the vampire killings attributed to VII are not done by the hands of any of those covenants, as the true criminals simply use VII as a scapegoat. It is not as much that there is no VII as much as everyone are VII- it is just that the eight groups above are more regularly blamed to be VII than the others because of their practices. <br /> <br /> Who was the first one to use VII as a symbol, however, is unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T14:59:33-07:00","id":1205767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205754#post1205754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah. I imagine that even in settings where VII is a proper covenant, they get a lot of copycats, to the point where <i>most</i> VII murders turn out to be false leads. I like the idea of a lot of vampires taking that to mean that there is no VII. Which, of course, the real VII uses to its advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I agree on that idea. I've just never found a proper reason to use VII as some ancient conspiracy in my games. It's actually been awhile since I've used VII in a game, so I might bring it in at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T17:35:25-07:00","id":1205835,"title":"","content":"So after rereading <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2081_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2081\" data-vbnamecard=\"2081\">Howalt</a> 's post I decided to handle Belial's Brood as if it's a cult, so that members of the Brood can still get Status in other covenants. Basically the Brood will act more like an undercover, underground conspiracy with the goal to infiltrate and disrupt Kindred society (while also doing less subtle direct terrorist attacks, obviously pinning those on the Carthians).<br /> <br /> I used Howalt's suggestions but slightly tweaked them. These are the Mystery Cult Initiation merit benefits I came up with for Belial's Brood. Please let me know if this is solid or perhaps too overpowered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mystery Cult initiation - Belial's Brood</span></span></b><br /> \u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Occult (Strix) specialty for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Atrocious, Cutthroat <i>or</i> Enticing merit for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Indomitable merit for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Riding the Wave Style (</span></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">) merit for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain a free dot in both composure and resolve (this cannot raise the attribute above 5). You can no longer have Touchstones.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-11-2018, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:36:35-07:00","id":1205899,"title":"","content":"Cheers! Flattered, truly.<br /> <br /> There is a problem of ambiguity in the formulation of the no touchstones drawback. Is that no attached touchstones or no touchstones at all? If the latter, that\u2019d mean Languid\u2019d come into play. Which is pretty crippling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:21:39-07:00","id":1206040,"title":"","content":"That's a really good point. I totally forgot about the Languid condition.<br /> <br /> So, here's a revision:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mystery Cult initiation - Belial's Brood</span></span></b><br /> \u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Occult (Strix) specialty for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Atrocious, Cutthroat <i>or</i> Enticing merit for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Indomitable merit for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain the Riding the Wave Style (</span></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">) merit for free.</span></span><br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Gain a free dot in both 'Composure' and 'Resolve' (this can raise the attribute above 5 <i>only</i> if you have 'Blood Potency' 6 or higher). Your 'Humanity' can never be higher than 5. You are not allowed to have the 'Touchstones' merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Given the nature of the Brood and the fact that they don't care about humanity, a lot of them will become draugrs. But I think there should be a way out for Belial's Brood members. So I came up with this merit:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Become one with the Beast (</b></span></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: <b><span style=\"color:#404040\">Mystery Cult initiation - Belial's Brood </span>\u2022</b> </i><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As a member of the Brood, you learned how to harness the Beast inside you and become one with it. When you drop to 'Humanity' 0, you do not become a draugr and do not lose control over yourself. Although you still become a slave to your Beast's desires, you are able to steer those desires as if you are 'Riding the Wave'. When at 'Humanity' 0, you are technically always in frenzy, but also always 'Riding the Wave'. As well; you are allowed to regain 'Humanity' by spending experience, even when you are at 'Humanity' 0.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Becoming one with the Beast means you have trouble staying in touch with your humanity. While you have this merit, buying back 'Humanity' with experience always costs 3 experience per dot. As well; when you are at 'Humanity' 0, Kindred outside of the Brood will not recognize the difference between a draugr and you; and willt treat you as any ordinary draugr.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:54:42-07:00","id":1206056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1205899#post1205899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cheers! Flattered, truly.<br /> <br /> There is a problem of ambiguity in the formulation of the no touchstones drawback. Is that no attached touchstones or no touchstones at all? If the latter, that\u2019d mean Languid\u2019d come into play. Which is pretty crippling.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Languid Condition is brought on by <i>losing</i> your last Touchstone, not by having no Touchstones. Also, there is prescedent for this \u201cyou are no longer able to maintain Touchstones\u201d effect, in the form of the Pledge to the Worthless One Ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T09:59:13-07:00","id":1206057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1206056#post1206056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Languid Condition is brought on by <i>losing</i> your last Touchstone, not by having no Touchstones. Also, there is prescedent for this \u201cyou are no longer able to maintain Touchstones\u201d effect, in the form of the Pledge to the Worthless One Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for that clarification! Given the fact that Belial's Brood shuns humanity, I thought it would make sense for them to not maintain their Touchstones. So I think it would make sense for a high-ranking Brood member to not have any Touchstones at all. Good to know that this is indeed possible without always suffering from the Languid condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T11:40:17-07:00","id":1206104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1206040#post1206040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Become one with the Beast (</b>[/FONT][/COLOR]\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: <b><span style=\"color:#404040\">Mystery Cult initiation - Belial's Brood </span>\u2022</b> </i><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As a member of the Brood, you learned how to harness the Beast inside you and become one with it. When you drop to 'Humanity' 0, you do not become a draugr and do not lose control over yourself. Although you still become a slave to your Beast's desires, you are able to steer those desires as if you are 'Riding the Wave'. When at 'Humanity' 0, you are technically always in frenzy, but also always 'Riding the Wave'. As well; you are allowed to regain 'Humanity' by spending experience, even when you are at 'Humanity' 0.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Becoming one with the Beast means you have trouble staying in touch with your humanity. While you have this merit, buying back 'Humanity' with experience always costs 3 experience per dot. As well; when you are at 'Humanity' 0, Kindred outside of the Brood will not recognize the difference between a draugr and you; and willt treat you as any ordinary draugr.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting and useful. Perhaps too useful, in the sense that if it's &quot;easy&quot; to do then everyone would want to join the cult and take the merit, no? Probably would require purchase of the merit only while sacrificing the last point of Humanity--falling off the edge and discovering you can fly by missing the ground, in other words.<br /> <br /> Not something your average vamp would tolerate even <i>attempting</i> for themselves, however.<br /> <br /> I have an NPC (a force of nature/plot NPC, frankly) who I'm theorizing managed to merge with a Strix in a fashion that subsumed it and thereby enabled both gaining control over his beast and avoiding the negative effects of Humanity 0. Fortunately the NPC in question is nominally a protagonist in comparison to the antagonist, and the strix I'm theorizing here was focused around the &quot;sloth&quot; vice.<br /> <br /> It's good not to have to pin down exactly why things are the way they are, sometimes.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T15:59:54-07:00","id":1206184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1206104#post1206104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting and useful. Perhaps too useful, in the sense that if it's &quot;easy&quot; to do then everyone would want to join the cult and take the merit, no? Probably would require purchase of the merit only while sacrificing the last point of Humanity--falling off the edge and discovering you can fly by missing the ground, in other words.<br /> <br /> Not something your average vamp would tolerate even <i>attempting</i> for themselves, however.<br /> <br /> I have an NPC (a force of nature/plot NPC, frankly) who I'm theorizing managed to merge with a Strix in a fashion that subsumed it and thereby enabled both gaining control over his beast and avoiding the negative effects of Humanity 0. Fortunately the NPC in question is nominally a protagonist in comparison to the antagonist, and the strix I'm theorizing here was focused around the &quot;sloth&quot; vice.<br /> <br /> It's good not to have to pin down exactly why things are the way they are, sometimes.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You are absolutely right. Of course one could say that the Brood doesn't just let anyone in on their secrets, nor do they allow anyone to leave the Brood. But you're right. I'll add your idea to the merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><b>Become one with the Beast (</b></span></span>\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites: <b><span style=\"color:#404040\">Mystery Cult initiation - Belial's Brood </span>\u2022</b>, 'Humanity' 0 (you must be able to purchase this merit at the moment your 'Humanity' drops to 0).</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As a member of the Brood, you learned how to harness the Beast inside you and become one with it. When you drop to 'Humanity' 0, you do not become a draugr and do not lose control over yourself. Although you still become a slave to your Beast's desires, you are able to steer those desires as if you are 'Riding the Wave'. When at 'Humanity' 0, you are technically always in frenzy, but also always 'Riding the Wave'. As well; you are allowed to regain 'Humanity' by spending experience, even when you are at 'Humanity' 0.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Becoming one with the Beast means you have trouble staying in touch with your humanity. While you have this merit, buying back 'Humanity' with experience always costs 3 experience per dot. As well; when you are at 'Humanity' 0, Kindred outside of the Brood will not recognize the difference between a draugr and you; and willt treat you as any ordinary draugr.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T17:46:43-07:00","id":1206203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1206056#post1206056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Languid Condition is brought on by <i>losing</i> your last Touchstone, not by having no Touchstones. Also, there is prescedent for this \u201cyou are no longer able to maintain Touchstones\u201d effect, in the form of the Pledge to the Worthless One Ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potatoes, tomatoes.<br /> <br /> Unless the vampire has already lost their last Touchstone, the ambiguity remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T17:53:23-07:00","id":1206206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1206203#post1206203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potatoes, tomatoes.<br /> <br /> Unless the vampire has already lost their last Touchstone, the ambiguity remains.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s really not ambiguous. At the time that you lose your last Touchstone, you must find another one within a month or gain the Languid Condition. Falling into Torpor resolves the Languid Condition. When you wake from Torpor, you have no Touchstones, but do not regain the Languid Condition again because you have not lost a Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:15:45-07:00","id":1206211,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll refer you tovearlier in the thread, where there already was confusion about the pledge.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the reformulation has fixed the issue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 04-12-2018, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T06:19:22-07:00","id":1206405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1206184#post1206184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are absolutely right. Of course one could say that the Brood doesn't just let anyone in on their secrets, nor do they allow anyone to leave the Brood. But you're right. I'll add your idea to the merit.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent, looks highly usable and ... something that senior folks in the Covenants would be terrified that the general populace knew about. Were there an easy way to dispense with the need to maintain Humanity it would tear down many premises of their society and move the needle much closer to the day when the world is ruled by draugr (kinda) and humans huddle in fear if not pens.<br /> <br /> Well. That's what the Strix dream of, anyway. If they dream. (<i>Do Strix Dream Of Shadowed Sheep?</i>)<br /> <br /> Stuff like this can become the sort of secret that once your character knows it, never lets them rest again from the raw paranoia.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T13:58:09-07:00","id":1207007,"title":"","content":"one could argue their redundant with the strix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T14:13:04-07:00","id":1207010,"title":"","content":"One could argue they're not. Just because they have overlap in evoking paranoia doesn't mean they're redundant. Vampires infiltrating vampire Covenants in the name of a demon evokes a very different feeling than near impervious, non-human entities that possess people because they like to spread chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:02:39-07:00","id":1207637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1207010#post1207010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could argue they're not. Just because they have overlap in evoking paranoia doesn't mean they're redundant. Vampires infiltrating vampire Covenants in the name of a demon evokes a very different feeling than near impervious, non-human entities that possess people because they like to spread chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with Tessie. The Strix are a particular type of antagonist and not necessarily suited to every chronicle. They're supposed to be at least somewhat unknowable, and stand in for Horrors in VtR versus core CofD.<br /> <br /> Masquerade had the two mega-factions as antagonists, which VtR lacks and instead hews to a more personal, local flavor. The Brood are an Other within all that. The lurking terror of selling yourself to power, versus the Strix's manipulation and/or outright possession. Brood are there because they belong and have become; Strix-possessed corpses are there because they are invading aliens.<br /> <br /> It's a very different flavor for your paranoia--not that'd I'd recommend limiting your options... go rainbow sherbet on your PC with this stuff.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 04-16-2018, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T14:02:14-07:00","id":1209394,"title":"","content":"I decided to slightly alter the Mystery Cult Initiation merit I homebrewed for Belial's Brood.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is the Belial's Brood cult initiation merit for my game now, feel free to use it:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mystery Cult Initiation - Belial's Brood</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022 Gain the Occult (the Beast) specialty for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022 Gain the Atrocious, Cutthroat </span></span><i>or</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Enticing merit for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain the Indomitable merit for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain the Riding the Wave Style (\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Gain the first dot in Coil of the Wyrm, 'Stir the Beast', for free, even when you aren't part of the Ordo Dracul. Your Humanity can never be higher than 5. You are not allowed to have the Touchstones merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> For extra clarification: The 5th dot in Mystery Cult Initiation - Belial's Brood does not allow you to purchase higher ranks in Coil of the Wyrm when you aren't a member of the Ordo Dracul. It only gives you the 1st dot, it does not allow you to then buy the 2nd to 5th dots. Only members of the Ordo Dracul can do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Feel free to give feedback!</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-20-2018, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:19:03-07:00","id":1210447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1209394#post1209394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mystery Cult Initiation - Belial's Brood</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022 Gain the Occult (the Beast) specialty for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022 Gain the Atrocious, Cutthroat </span></span><i>or</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Enticing merit for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain the Indomitable merit for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain the Riding the Wave Style (\u2022\u2022\u2022) merit for free.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Gain the first dot in Coil of the Wyrm, 'Stir the Beast', for free, even when you aren't part of the Ordo Dracul. Your Humanity can never be higher than 5. You are not allowed to have the Touchstones merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> For extra clarification: The 5th dot in Mystery Cult Initiation - Belial's Brood does not allow you to purchase higher ranks in Coil of the Wyrm when you aren't a member of the Ordo Dracul. It only gives you the 1st dot, it does not allow you to then buy the 2nd to 5th dots. Only members of the Ordo Dracul can do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> Feel free to give feedback!</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You will want to carefully double-check that Stir the Beast actually permits you to use Riding the Wave Style at the same time. A quick search found some posts from 2014 on these forums implying no, that they are different things. <br /> <br /> An alternate way to gain what seems to be the intent (easy frenzy riding) could be to simply at 5 dots &quot;reduce successes needed to initiate Riding the Wave to 1.&quot; That would still require the Willpower expenditure and roll, risking failure (and Dramatic Failure), without muddling things up with Coil of the Wyrm+clarifications. <br /> <br /> It seems, by the way, that one could take Mystery Cult Initiation - Belial's Brood, without going through the Thebian ritual reference earlier in the thread. I assume that is intentional and would make the cult both more accessible and more appealing to mainstream vamps. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hey mate, want a flyer? Join our club and learn about yer beast and how to keep it happy and off yer back!&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T09:30:17-07:00","id":1210457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210447#post1210447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You will want to carefully double-check that Stir the Beast actually permits you to use Riding the Wave Style at the same time. A quick search found some posts from 2014 on these forums implying no, that they are different things.<br /> <br /> An alternate way to gain what seems to be the intent (easy frenzy riding) could be to simply at 5 dots &quot;reduce successes needed to initiate Riding the Wave to 1.&quot; That would still require the Willpower expenditure and roll, risking failure (and Dramatic Failure), without muddling things up with Coil of the Wyrm+clarifications.<br /> <br /> It seems, by the way, that one could take Mystery Cult Initiation - Belial's Brood, without going through the Thebian ritual reference earlier in the thread. I assume that is intentional and would make the cult both more accessible and more appealing to mainstream vamps.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey mate, want a flyer? Join our club and learn about yer beast and how to keep it happy and off yer back!&quot;<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> I have a question:<br /> <br /> Isn't &quot;Riding the Wave&quot; something you can try to do every single time the GM tells you to roll for frenzy? I thought Riding the Wave is something you can attempt every single time you're close to going into frenzy (e.g. every time you have to roll a Resolve + Composure for it). With 'Stir the Beast' you'd give the player more control over that, by allowing the player to provoke frenzy in himself whenever he feels like by spending a point of Willpower. He'd be able to spend a willpower to provoke frenzy in himself, and then be able to to attempt Riding the Wave. Is this not correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T12:33:20-07:00","id":1210545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210457#post1210457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> I have a question:<br /> <br /> Isn't &quot;Riding the Wave&quot; something you can try to do every single time the GM tells you to roll for frenzy? I thought Riding the Wave is something you can attempt every single time you're close to going into frenzy (e.g. every time you have to roll a Resolve + Composure for it). With 'Stir the Beast' you'd give the player more control over that, by allowing the player to provoke frenzy in himself whenever he feels like by spending a point of Willpower. He'd be able to spend a willpower to provoke frenzy in himself, and then be able to to attempt Riding the Wave. Is this not correct?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can ride the wave when you are provoked to make a frenzy check. Stir the Beast specifically states (now that I've compared the two) that the frenzy that results is an &quot;involuntary frenzy (p.103)&quot;--except you get to specify the target/goal. That last bit makes it functionally identical to riding the wave, however the Merit style will not apply since it is, technically, not riding....<br /> <br /> If your objective is to have a power that enables one to just enter frenzy whenever at cost of 1 Willpower, then simply say &quot;may expend 1 Willpower to provoke an immediate frenzy check in self; the expended Willpower counts as well for activation of Riding the Wave, if desired.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could also houserule that the style applies to activation of the Coil as well, if you wish. RAW they do not, however.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:25:16-07:00","id":1210949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210545#post1210545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can ride the wave when you are provoked to make a frenzy check. Stir the Beast specifically states (now that I've compared the two) that the frenzy that results is an &quot;involuntary frenzy (p.103)&quot;--except you get to specify the target/goal. That last bit makes it functionally identical to riding the wave, however the Merit style will not apply since it is, technically, not riding....<br /> <br /> If your objective is to have a power that enables one to just enter frenzy whenever at cost of 1 Willpower, then simply say &quot;may expend 1 Willpower to provoke an immediate frenzy check in self; the expended Willpower counts as well for activation of Riding the Wave, if desired.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could also houserule that the style applies to activation of the Coil as well, if you wish. RAW they do not, however.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get that Stir the Beast in and of itself is not the same as Riding the Wave. However, my question was; can I not first Stir the Beast and <i>then</i> attempt at turning it into Riding the Wave by going through the whole ordeal of spending Willpower and rolling Resolve + Composure checks like you would with any other frenzy provocation?<br /> <br /> The way I see it; Stir the Beast works like an involuntary frenzy provocation (except it really is voluntary, but mechanically it's involuntary). That means you can attempt to hold off the frenzy and try to control it by spending Willpower and rolling Resolve + Composure (as written on page 105 under 'Riding the Wave').<br /> <br /> Basically, Stir the Beast gives the user some control over when he's going to be provoked into a frenzy. I see no reason why this user then cannot try to grab that frenzy by the reins and turn it into a Riding the Wave just like with any other frenzy provocation. If you read the 2nd to 5th dots from Coil of the Wyrm, it seems highly likely that Stir the Beast is meant to be used this way. Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:36:58-07:00","id":1210951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210949#post1210949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stir the Beast works like an involuntary frenzy provocation (except it really is voluntary, but mechanically it's involuntary).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a provocation. You go directly to Frenzy, and you can only attempt to Ride the Wave when you otherwise would've attempted to resist Frenzy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I think it's a common house rule to allow Riding the Wave in combination with Stir the Beast. We do it. Otherwise you get two mutually exclusive benefits from Coil of the Wyrm when the design philosophy for second edition has been for later dots to expand upon or complement the previous dots.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another house rule we have is that we don't award beats for using Stir the Beast unless you use it to redirect a natural Frenzy. Otherwise it's a relatively safe (since you can choose target) WP to Beat converter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2018, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T07:43:02-07:00","id":1210954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210951#post1210951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a provocation. You go directly to Frenzy, and you can only attempt to Ride the Wave when you otherwise would've attempted to resist Frenzy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand I think it's a common house rule to allow Riding the Wave in combination with Stir the Beast. We do it. Otherwise you get two mutually exclusive benefits from Coil of the Wyrm when the design philosophy for second edition has been for later dots to expand upon or complement the previous dots.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another house rule we have is that we don't award beats for using Stir the Beast unless you use it to redirect a natural Frenzy. Otherwise it's a relatively safe (since you can choose target) WP to Beat converter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I think I wanna houserule it that way then. Unless there are other ways for a vampire to provoke a frenzy in himself so he can then attempt to Ride the Wave?<br /> <br /> Because that's what I want really, at least for the Belial's Brood members, to give them the option to provoke frenzy in themselves whenever they want so they can attempt to Ride the Wave whenever they want. Otherwise, the 'Ride the Wave (Style)' merit seems rather... situational.<br /> <br /> Or do I misunderstand Riding the Wave completely? Is it something you can do whenever you want, or only when you're provoked into a frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T08:06:33-07:00","id":1210959,"title":"","content":"Riding the Wave can only be done as an alternative to resisting Frenzy.<br /> <br /> The easiest way would be to use the house rule I presented (especially if other characters will use the Coil of the Wyrm). However, you might want to rephrase the fifth dot of MCI as just granting the benefits of Stir the Beast rather than the actual Coil dot. For Ordo characters, once you've learned the first dot in your first Mystery you're able to develop the rest of the dots (or possibly alternatives) on your own.<br /> If you're worried about stacking XP costs for the same benefit, you could also include a one XP discount/refund for Stir the Beast (motivated by understanding the underlying principles of the Coil).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2018, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T08:16:50-07:00","id":1210962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210959#post1210959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Riding the Wave can only be done as an alternative to resisting Frenzy.<br /> <br /> The easiest way would be to use the house rule I presented (especially if other characters will use the Coil of the Wyrm). However, you might want to rephrase the fifth dot of MCI as just granting the benefits of Stir the Beast rather than the actual Coil dot. For Ordo characters, once you've learned the first dot in your first Mystery you're able to develop the rest of the dots (or possibly alternatives) on your own.<br /> If you're worried about stacking XP costs for the same benefit, you could also include a one XP discount for Stir the Beast (motivated by understanding the underlying principles of the Coil).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I was thinking about giving each dot in MCI at least 2 options. I like it when players get choices. For example a player might already get 'Riding the Wave (Style)' before getting to the 3rd dot of MCI - Belial's Brood and feel like getting the 3rd dot in MCI is a waste of experience. Same for Ordo Dracul members and the 5th dot of MCI - Belial's Brood.<br /> <br /> I dunno if the MCI merit is supposed to be this good, but I do feel like every dot should feel like it's worth your time, that's my design philosophy when I'm homebrewing at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T09:22:43-07:00","id":1210982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210962#post1210962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example a player might already get 'Riding the Wave (Style)' before getting to the 3rd dot of MCI - Belial's Brood and feel like getting the 3rd dot in MCI is a waste of experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually already handled by Sanctity of Merits. The player gets their already invested Merit dots back to spend on other Merits (or back as XP if the ST allows it).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210962#post1210962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno if the MCI merit is supposed to be this good, but I do feel like every dot should feel like it's worth your time, that's my design philosophy when I'm homebrewing at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. Especially the latter, supernatural dots. For vampires that could be a source of Supernatural Merits they otherwise can't have (except for Zirnitra-Ordo; those cheaters). Or other non-standard benefits. For example, I'm working on an Underworld focused MCI for vampires. This is the WIP version of my fifth dot:<br /> <br /> &quot;Kerberos (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): The Underworld is not just mastered, but an extension of the Kerberos. He feels as at home in the depths as a predator in its own lair. Take a modified version of Direction Sense (Advanced) (BtP p.114). While in the Underworld the Kerberos always knows which way is closest to all Domains, Rivers and Avernian Gates he has encountered.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps not as potent as a Discipline or Coil dot (in fact, it's technically underpowered compared to the guidelines) it's extremely useful, and I don't see a way for either Kindred or mortals to gain a similar benefit.<br /> Notes: Kerberos is the title associated with that dot. An Underworld-version of the non-Advanced Direction Sense is already granted by a previous dot. (If the character also has the regular Direction Sense, they get +2 to all rolls to navigate the Underworld since the regular benefit can't stack.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:18:00-07:00","id":1211118,"title":"","content":"Isn't stiring the beast more of targeted frenzy, that you can invoke at anytime or when you fail riding the wave you can use it control the frenzy somewhat. While riding the wave means your complety in control of the frenzy, which means its power boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T13:40:45-07:00","id":1211134,"title":"","content":"If you've failed Riding the Wave then you've already entered Frenzy (and a bad one at that). Stir the Beast can only be done before you're in Frenzy. Though it's possible to use Stir the Beast in the middle of rolling for Riding the Wave, if you want to stop rolling without having to fall into the dramatic failure kind of Frenzy.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flazeo25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211118#post1211118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IWhile riding the wave means your complety in control of the frenzy, which means its power boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Riding the Wave doesn't give you any power boost compared to regular Frenzy, unless you have the Riding the Wave Style Merit. Unfortunately it's of limited use for characters who study the Coil of the Wyrm. The third dot of the Coil completely negates the third and fourth dot of the Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2018, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:00:53-07:00","id":1211146,"title":"","content":"By power boost I mean you in control of the beast for the scene so that's well better than your character killing random passerbys on street.<br /> <br /> Also the fourth and fifth dot can still be used when riding the wave so you with 5 dots you can stay frenzyed for as long as you want and end it at scene end or your death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","user":"flazeo25","date":". 04-24-2018, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T14:34:53-07:00","id":1211160,"title":"","content":"You don't get control for a whole scene. You get to choose the target of the Frenzy, but once you've chosen it's identical to an uncontrolled Frenzy (except any benefits gained from the Riding the Wave Style). Walking around random passerbys instead of tearing through them still requires spending WP. Stir the Beast and Riding the Wave are basically identical with the exception of that Merit.<br /> That said, that's not how my group plays Riding the Wave. We've house ruled that extra control (being able to walk around non-targets, for example) because that's more interesting to us, and keeps Riding the Wave relevant to characters with Coil of the Wyrm. Especially since the third dot would be nigh useless otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flazeo25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211146#post1211146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the fourth and fifth dot can still be used when riding the wave so you with 5 dots you can stay frenzyed for as long as you want and end it at scene end or your death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstood. The third and fourth dot of Riding the Wave Style is useless for someone with Coil of the Wyrm 3+. They both modifies spending WP to attempt to Ride, but Wyrm 3 removes the WP cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-24-2018, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T15:17:27-07:00","id":1211177,"title":"","content":"So going 3 dots in ride the wave pointless if you have 5 dots in coil of wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:49:45-07:00","id":1211242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210951#post1210951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise you get two mutually exclusive benefits from Coil of the Wyrm when the design philosophy for second edition has been for later dots to expand upon or complement the previous dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, the primary benefit of Stir the Beast is that it lets you steer a frenzy without having to engage with the usual set of desires the Beast answers to, and Leash the Beast serves its main benefit by changing riding the wave from a more expensive way to redirect frenzy than Stir the Beast to a less expensive but more risky way to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>flazeo25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211177#post1211177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So going 3 dots in ride the wave pointless if you have 5 dots in coil of wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, yes, but on the other hand, having five dots in Coil of the Wyrm requires that you either have that one Coil as your chosen Mystery or be at the upper echelons of the Ordo Dracul, and it still calls for the expenditure of a lot more Experiences than a Merit whose entry requirements are pretty much the expected fare for a fighting style built around a state unlocked with a Resolve + Composure roll \u2014 Beast's Power accomplishes some of the effects of Riding 5 without an extra cost as part of a larger package, and that's about what I'd expect the relation to be between a Style Merit built specifically around riding the wave as a combat methodology and a major mystical alteration of the vampiric condition with the specific aim of making the thing that drives frenzy more effective and controllable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-24-2018, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T03:07:43-07:00","id":1211342,"title":"","content":"Other way around. It's the third dot of Wyrm that makes the third and fourth dot worthless (and by extension making the fifth dot more expensive).<br /> <br /> Wyrm 1 vs 3; well, I can only speak for my group, but without being able to combine those dots (as well as house ruling that extra benefit from Riding) we'd almost never use Leash the Beast. The risk for dramatic Frenzy is alone not worth it in many cases, and having to wait 1+ turns in combat before you enter Frenzy can be very dangerous. Especially since Wyrm 4 grants extra Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T06:52:56-07:00","id":1211394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210954#post1210954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think I wanna houserule it that way then. Unless there are other ways for a vampire to provoke a frenzy in himself so he can then attempt to Ride the Wave?<br /> <br /> Because that's what I want really, at least for the Belial's Brood members, to give them the option to provoke frenzy in themselves whenever they want so they can attempt to Ride the Wave whenever they want. Otherwise, the 'Ride the Wave (Style)' merit seems rather... situational.<br /> <br /> Or do I misunderstand Riding the Wave completely? Is it something you can do whenever you want, or only when you're provoked into a frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the conflicts uncovered here, you may be best served to use your own text and make it exactly what you want from the MCI. Which, for the fifth dot can/should be something specific and unique.<br /> <br /> In this case &quot;you may choose to frenzy at will as an instant action&quot; would cover the objective, without negating the usefulness of Riding the Wave style, Wyrm, or the need to spend Willpower and roll to ride per RAW.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T10:14:56-07:00","id":1211457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1210954#post1210954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or do I misunderstand Riding the Wave completely? Is it something you can do whenever you want, or only when you're provoked into a frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure the intent is that you can ride the wave at any time, whether or not you are currently being provoked to Frenzy. It worked that way through all of 1e, and the text of 2e doesn't seem to me to preclude that possibility. It\u2019s been a subject of some debate around here. As has the possibility of combining Riding the Wave and Coil of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be clear, I\u2019m in the \u201cYou can always attempt to Ride the Wave\u201d camp and the \u201cStir the Beast is not the same as Riding the Wave and therefore doesn\u2019t work with the Riding the Wave Fighting Style\u201d camp. But I have seen compelling arguments for both sides of both arguments, and I think both ultimately come down to a question of what works best at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-25-2018, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:10:39-07:00","id":1211666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211457#post1211457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure the intent is that you can ride the wave at any time, whether or not you are currently being provoked to Frenzy. It worked that way through all of 1e</div> </div> </div> </div>Did it? The nearest I can find in 1e Core is that you were able to <i>end</i> the frenzy at any time if you rode the wave, and the only consequences of failure were falling into ordinary frenzy and not getting anything out of the point of Willpower you spent to try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T23:19:06-07:00","id":1211700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211666#post1211666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did it? The nearest I can find in 1e Core is that you were able to <i>end</i> the frenzy at any time if you rode the wave, and the only consequences of failure were falling into ordinary frenzy and not getting anything out of the point of Willpower you spent to try.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Under some circumstances, characters might want to <b>frenzy on purpose</b>. For all the horror of what a character might do in frenzy, succumbing to the Beast carries power. The great difficulty lies in controlling one\u2019s actions so that the Beast achieves something useful. Young Kindred call such a temporary, negotiated surrender to the Beast riding the wave. Older Kindred call it damnable foolishness.<br /> <br /> If a character wants to ride the wave, the player makes Resolve + Composure rolls and tries to accumulate successes as an extended action, just like fighting back frenzy. In this case, however, <b>the vampire tries to goad the Beast while supplying it with a target of the Man\u2019s choice</b>. The player also expends a Willpower point for trying to direct the frenzy in advance. Riding the wave always requires accumulating at least five successes. The Storyteller may ask for more, or modify the Resolve + Composure rolls depending on how well the desired task accords with the character\u2019s personality or existing emotions. For instance, a character probably has little trouble <b>deliberately frenzying</b> when he faces the Lupine that murdered two of his Kindred allies. On the other hand, frenzying so he might have a better chance to climb up a building almost certainly doesn\u2019t work. If the player fails one of the Resolve + Composure rolls, the character falls into an undirected frenzy. </div> </div> </div>Bolded for emphasis. Frenzying in the absence of provocation was pretty much the whole point of Riding the Wave in 1e. I\u2019ll concede that it\u2019s debatable whether or not the intent is for Riding the Wave to be possible absent a Frenzy trigger in 2e, but I think in 1e it\u2019s quite clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T03:37:44-07:00","id":1211727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211700#post1211700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolded for emphasis.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I read language like &quot;succumbing to the Beast&quot; and &quot;negotiated surrender&quot; and &quot;goad the Beast&quot; as &quot;use a normal frenzy stimulus and steer from there,&quot; not &quot;vampires can literally enter the state of frenzy at the drop of a hat if they feel like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frenzy triggers were still broad enough that you could gin one up deliberately, but there's a pretty stark narrative distinction between &quot;a vampire can take a moment to let their anger and desperation flow through them from an appropriate pretext to get the benefits of frenzy in semi-controlled conditions&quot; and &quot;a vampire can enter frenzy completely without provocation at all,&quot; even if the practical outcome is still &quot;the character enters the state of frenzy knowing that they will do so ahead of time.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 2e especially, where frenzy works a little differently and the process is expressly a reflexive action that doesn't interfere with your ability to do something else in the same turn, I think it's important to understand the difference in framing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T06:22:01-07:00","id":1211763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211727#post1211727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I read language like &quot;succumbing to the Beast&quot; and &quot;negotiated surrender&quot; and &quot;goad the Beast&quot; as &quot;use a normal frenzy stimulus and steer from there,&quot; not &quot;vampires can literally enter the state of frenzy at the drop of a hat if they feel like it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, \u201cnegotiates surrender\u201d was one I almost bolded. I think the text makes it clear that some kind of negative emotional stimulus is required, but I think it\u2019s also pretty clear that such stimulus need not be a Frenzy trigger. I wouldn\u2019t think simply seeing a werewolf who killed two of your allies would necessarily force a Frenzy check, and I wouldn\u2019t describe taking control of a Frenzy that\u2019s about to happen anyway as \u201cFrenzying on purpose.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211727#post1211727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frenzy triggers were still broad enough that you could gin one up deliberately, but there's a pretty stark narrative distinction between &quot;a vampire can take a moment to let their anger and desperation flow through them from an appropriate pretext to get the benefits of frenzy in semi-controlled conditions&quot; and &quot;a vampire can enter frenzy completely without provocation at all,&quot; even if the practical outcome is still &quot;the character enters the state of frenzy knowing that they will do so ahead of time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But that\u2019s not what it says the vampire does. It says she tries to deliberately goad the beast while providing it with a target of the man\u2019s choice. Why would you need to goad a beast that\u2019s already raring to attack? Sure, she needs a provocation of some sort - she can\u2019t just Frenzy to help her climb up a building - but the language does not make it sound to me as if the required provocation has to be grounds for a Frenzy check. In fact if it did, it would be pretty hard to \u201cspend a Willpower point... in advance.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211727#post1211727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e especially, where frenzy works a little differently and the process is expressly a reflexive action that doesn't interfere with your ability to do something else in the same turn, I think it's important to understand the difference in framing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can see an argument for Riding the Wave requiring a preexisting Frenzy trigger in 2e, even if I don\u2019t think the rules text really makes that explicit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:49:27-07:00","id":1211825,"title":"","content":"I mean, it's called &quot;Ride the Wave.&quot; This implies there has to be a wave to ride. I've always been in the &quot;response to a Frenzy trigger&quot; camp, and feel that the two options are significantly different in tone, though I'm not so attached to the idea that I wouldn't change if we ever got an official answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:27:12-07:00","id":1211847,"title":"","content":"I'm with Charlaquin interpetation on this topic but I can see that in 2ed, riding the wave, could be mechanically intended as needing a pre-existing stimulus. <br /> But I would also say that, every situation that really matter and would be needed of a riding the way, represent a stimulus:<br /> - escaping from hunters/werewolf (you are risking your life...)<br /> - fighting hunter/werewolf (again, you are risking your life)<br /> - your prey is running away from you (what a shame if you'd fail the hunt)<br /> - take your hand close to a candle (fire)<br /> - trapped in a building needing the power of the Beast to destroy a wall (you are trapped, isn't it a sufficient stimulus?)<br /> <br /> Now; I need to get into a building jumping to the first block without any pressure. Maybe that's not a direct stimulus, but isn't the Beast always lurking from the vampire very depth, waiting her occasion to get free? Why she cannot free herself, if the vampire deliberately choose to let her free?<br /> The stimulus are there just to give the beast an edge to win against the vampire will. But if the kin want to let her free, why the Beast shouldn't take advantage of it? There is always a big drawback if you choose to go with this; you could lose the roll and the control. So it's not just a Jolly card to play whenever you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-26-2018, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:17:46-07:00","id":1211871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211825#post1211825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's called &amp;quot;Ride the Wave.&amp;quot; This implies there has to be a wave to ride.</div> </div> </div> </div>This argument has never been compelling to me, because a.) it\u2019s just a name and b.) who\u2019s to say you can\u2019t <i>make</i> a Wave to Ride?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211825#post1211825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always been in the &amp;quot;response to a Frenzy trigger&amp;quot; camp, and feel that the two options are significantly different in tone, though I'm not so attached to the idea that I wouldn't change if we ever got an official answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with Marcus - pretty much any time you would <i>want</i> to Frenzy, there should be ample stimuli to trigger one, so I don\u2019t really see a significant difference in tone. The only practical difference I see is that the \u201cresponse to a Frenzy trigger\u201d interpretation means a player needs ST permission to Ride the Wave. If the player has agency to decide when a stimulus would trigger Frenzy, then there\u2019s no practical difference between the two interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:45:02-07:00","id":1212131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1211871#post1211871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t really see a significant difference in tone</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference in tone is as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) If you can Ride the Wave at any time, then it is akin to letting the Beast off its leash whenever you need it. Locked door? Don't need to pick it. Just let the Beast off its leash to break it down. The Beast becomes a tool that serves you, though it is certainly still risky.<br /> 2) If you can only Ride the Wave in response to Frenzy, then the Beast is an unrelenting force you cannot control, merely <i>attempt </i>to steer towards a less destructive end. It will never be a boon you can call up whenever you need it, but always a curse that you can only hope to mitigate somewhat.<br /> <br /> The tonal shift is a matter of control. Are you controlling the Beast, or does the Beast control you, and the most you can hope to do is redirect it? I find the latter far more thematic, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1692,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","user":"Maina","date":". 04-26-2018, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T23:24:12-07:00","id":1212163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1212131#post1212131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference in tone is as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) If you can Ride the Wave at any time, then it is akin to letting the Beast off its leash whenever you need it. Locked door? Don't need to pick it. Just let the Beast off its leash to break it down. The Beast becomes a tool that serves you, though it is certainly still risky.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s one way to put it. Another would be that the beast is constantly seething just beneath the surface, and that all it takes to let it out is to stop actively holding it back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1198700-belial-s-brood-in-2nd-edition?p=1212131#post1212131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If you can only Ride the Wave in response to Frenzy, then the Beast is an unrelenting force you cannot control, merely <i>attempt </i>to steer towards a less destructive end. It will never be a boon you can call up whenever you need it, but always a curse that you can only hope to mitigate somewhat.<br /> <br /> The tonal shift is a matter of control. Are you controlling the Beast, or does the Beast control you, and the most you can hope to do is redirect it? I find the latter far more thematic, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t ever describe Riding the Wave as controlling the Beast, whether or not it\u2019s possible to do without the Storyteller asking for a Frenzy check first. At best, you\u2019re pointing it at something you want to fuck up and <i>hoping</i> that\u2019s the only thing it destroys before you manage to wrangle it again. The question for me isn\u2019t \u201cdo you control the beast or does the beast control you?\u201d the question is, \u201cis the beast dormant until something stirs it, or is it always one tiny slip up from taking over?\u201d<br /> <br /> And, again, even if you prefer the latter thematically, practically it makes no difference in any game where players have the agency to decide if something is a Frenzy trigger for their own character. And even in a game where the ST reserves the right to say, \u201cno, you aren\u2019t allowed to make a Frenzy check for that,\u201d all it does is insures PCs carry lighters with them all the time and potentially adds a point of aggravated damage as a tax on Riding the Wave when the ST doesn\u2019t think you should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-27-2018, 02:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}